{
  "$comment": [
    "Chronostratigraphic units and their base ages, from the ICS International",
    "Chronostratigraphic Chart. Read by tools/generate_precomputed.py to build",
    "the geologic-column view: each unit's secular span is converted through",
    "the calibrated model into a young-earth duration.",
    "",
    "The list mixes ranks on purpose, and matches how the column is usually",
    "drawn for this argument: the Quaternary and Neogene are split into epochs,",
    "because that is where the interesting compression happens, and everything",
    "older is given by period.",
    "",
    "`base_secular_age` is the OLDER boundary of the unit, in years. Units are",
    "listed youngest first; each unit's younger boundary is the previous unit's",
    "base, and the Holocene's is the present.",
    "",
    "PROVISIONAL: these are ICS v2023/09 values entered by hand and have not",
    "been checked against the published chart by a geologist. They are on the",
    "pre-publication checklist in frontend_plan.md."
  ],
